            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christina"
            },
            "reviewBody": "WOW, this was absolutely delicious! I have to admit, I did not have the highest hopes for this, but I am so glad I decided to give it a shot anyway. So simple to prepare and very light and refreshing. I made this exactly as written and would not change a thing. I put the cubes in a glass and piped on whipped cream and dusted it with cocoa powder. This recipe is a definate keeper that I will be making VERY often~YUM! Thanks for sharing. :)"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TrendyRum6813"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a keeper! I was a bit more generous with the sugar and I’m unsure if it’ll completely set up because I had trouble dissolving the gelatine, but I tried some after about 2 hours and it was so good! I added half and half along with cocoa powder and cinnamon on top, and it was great! This will be a regular in my house. Edit: I use Kcups to brew my coffee. I tried dissolving the gelatine (I used Knox brand) in about a quarter cup of freshly brewed coffee and it worked much better. The label on the Knox brand calls for a quarter cup as well. Something to consider :) I made a new batch because I ended up eating half of the one I had made! I put Starbucks cinnamon half&amp;half on top along with cinnnamon and cocoa powder. It added a perfect sweetness to the jelly. Yum!!",
            "datePublished": "2024-06-19T01:56:09.467Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lulu"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Every other reviewer kept calling this 'refreshing', and really, there's no other way to describe this tasty dessert. Perfect on a warm New England evening. It was so easy to make too! I used Splenda to sweeten it, and used Starbucks Caramel flavoured coffee. I poured it into little Irish coffee mugs to set, and topped it with whipped cream. They looked great and tasted even better than they looked! Simple, delicious, and yes, refreshing! Thanks so much for this recipe! I will be making this for me and for company over and over and over again!",
            "datePublished": "2012-03-23T18:21:05.613Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "M Stoffel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a really refreshing coffee jello I ate right out of the cups, no toppings required. I do love my coffee though. I used three single-serve packets of Splenda instead of sugar, which worked great. I'm always looking for a shortcut so instead of dissolving the gelatin separately I just mixed it into the warm coffee/splenda before it came to boiling on the stove. This seemed to work very well but I'm not familiar enough with gelatin to know if that's recommended or not. Thanks very much for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-20T08:10:44.800Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kat Brown"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is also delicious cubed and served in a martini glass with a Starbucks Doubleshot for breakfast, or with Bailey's Irish Cream as an after dinner treat. I add a dollop of whipped cream and shaved semisweet chocolate to mine.",
            "datePublished": "2020-08-30T21:28:27.123Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Keri"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent! I didn't have any whipped cream, ice cream, liquid coffee creamer, or chocolate sauce on hand, so I added about 2 Tbs of powdered vanilla flavored coffee creamer to the liquid before filling individual dessert glasses. My husband and I loved it as-is. My two daughters said they liked it, but would have liked it better if it was sweeter. Next time (and there will be MANY \"next times\"!) I'll pour out servings for my husband and myself, then add a little more sugar to the girls' servings. Can't wait to try it topped with whipped cream!",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-09T20:52:18.757Z"
          },
